  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1) \n\nLarge scale ridging builds into our west, heralding in northerly \nflow and a broad area of surface high pressure. This translates to \nquieter and cooler conditions, with highs on Sunday and Monday only \nreaching the low 80s, while overnight lows fall into the low \n60s/upper 50s. \n\nUnfortunately, this reprieve is short lived as the \nbulk of the ridge continues to push east into our area, bringing a \nreturn temperatures in the low 90s by mid week. Ensemble guidance has\ndecent consensus in a broad area of low pressure moving through the \nHudson Bay region mid week. This will bring a cold front down \nthrough the Great Lakes sometime around Wednesday into late week. While\ndetails regarding this system will be fine tuned over the coming \ndays, it looks like this could be our next chance for showers and \nstorms.",
